        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Nasdaq, Inc.; Citrix Systems; International Securities Exchange Holdings, Inc.\n- People: Ivers Whitman Riley\n- Organizations: NASDAQ; Hong Kong Futures Exchange\n- Places: Los Angeles, California; Savannah, Georgia; Europe\n- Concepts: financial services; stock exchanges; software; virtualization; SaaS; cloud computing\n\nFacts:\n- Ivers Whitman Riley was born on September 28, 1932, in Los Angeles, California.\n- Ivers Whitman Riley served as Chief Executive of the Hong Kong Futures Exchange from 1994 to 1997 and again from 1999 to 2000.\n- Ivers Whitman Riley served as Chairman of the International Securities Exchange from 2002 to 2006.\n- Nasdaq, Inc. is an American multinational financial services corporation that owns and operates the NASDAQ stock market and eight European stock exchanges.\n- International Securities Exchange Holdings, Inc. is a wholly owned subsidiary of Nasdaq, Inc..\n- Citrix Systems, Inc. is an American multinational software company that provides server, application, and desktop virtualization, networking, software as a service, and cloud computing technologies.\n- Ivers Whitman Riley died on February 17, 2015, in Savannah, Georgia.",
